From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bug NNNNNNN - Queue enough hardware-decoded VP9/AV1 frames to
 cover a multi-frame packet. r?media-playback-reviewers

MediaDecoderStateMachine keeps only media.video-queue.hw-accel-size (3)
decoded frames ahead when the decoder is hardware accelerated, on the
assumption that hardware decoding is fast for every frame. That holds per
decoded frame, but not per packet: a VP9 superframe or an AV1 temporal unit
of a hierarchical (pyramid) GOP carries the hidden ALTREF and the hidden
frames of every layer below it before the shown frame. The hardware
decoder (VA-API, V4L2, Vulkan) runs one job per frame, so that packet takes
several frame durations, and the next packets (show_existing_frame) come
out almost for free. With 3 frames queued, the queue runs dry during the
burst although the average decode rate keeps up.

Seen on an RK3588 (Hantro VPU981 behind libva-v4l2-request) with a 4K60
AV1 clip with 16-frame mini-GOPs: ~10 ms per decoded frame, but 6-7 frames
(~60 ms) in the first temporal unit of each mini-GOP. Firefox dropped 6.2%
and 3.1% of the frames in two runs; with media.video-queue.hw-accel-size=6
it dropped 2.4%, the same as the 1080p clips. Chrome drops 0.2% on the same
driver.

Report MinNumVideoBuffers = 8 from the Linux FFmpeg video decoder when it
decodes VP9 or AV1 in hardware (not in low-latency mode). A hidden frame is
only of use when it is kept in one of the 8 reference slots (and a VP9
superframe holds at most 8 frames), so 8 frames cover the longest burst a
real stream produces. The FFmpeg hardware frame pool already has room for
it (8 references + EXTRA_HW_FRAMES 9). The Android implementation of the
same property (MediaCodec output buffer limits) is unchanged; H.264/HEVC
decode one frame per packet and keep the 3-frame default.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp b/dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp
--- a/dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp
+++ b/dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp
@@ -2596,6 +2596,38 @@
       return MediaDataDecoder::GetDecodeProperty(aName);
   }
 }
+#elif defined(MOZ_USE_HWDECODE) && defined(MOZ_WIDGET_GTK)
+Maybe<MediaDataDecoder::PropertyValue> FFmpegVideoDecoder<
+    LIBAV_VER>::GetDecodeProperty(MediaDataDecoder::PropertyName aName) const {
+  if (aName != PropertyName::MinNumVideoBuffers || mLowLatency ||
+      !IsHardwareAccelerated()) {
+    return MediaDataDecoder::GetDecodeProperty(aName);
+  }
+  // A hardware decoder (VA-API, V4L2, Vulkan) decodes one frame per job, but
+  // a VP9 superframe or an AV1 temporal unit can carry several frames of
+  // which only the last one is shown: with hierarchical (pyramid) GOPs the
+  // first packet of a mini-GOP holds the hidden ALTREF and the hidden frames
+  // of every pyramid layer below it. The decoder spends several frame
+  // durations on that packet and then returns the following frames
+  // (show_existing_frame) almost for free. The default hardware queue
+  // (media.video-queue.hw-accel-size, 3 frames) is shorter than that burst,
+  // so 4K60 AV1 drops frames although the average decode rate keeps up.
+  // A hidden frame is only of use when it is kept in one of the 8 reference
+  // slots of VP9/AV1 (and a VP9 superframe holds at most 8 frames), so a
+  // queue of 8 frames covers the longest burst a real stream produces.
+  static constexpr uint32_t kMaxFramesPerPacket = 8;
+  switch (mCodecID) {
+#  ifdef FFMPEG_AV1_DECODE
+    case AV_CODEC_ID_AV1:
+#  endif
+    case AV_CODEC_ID_VP9:
+      FFMPEG_LOG("Hardware {} decoding: asking for at least {} queued frames",
+                 AVCodecToString(mCodecID), kMaxFramesPerPacket);
+      return Some(PropertyValue(kMaxFramesPerPacket));
+    default:
+      return MediaDataDecoder::GetDecodeProperty(aName);
+  }
+}
 #endif
 
 AVCodecID FFmpegVideoDecoder<LIBAV_VER>::GetCodecId(
diff --git a/dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.h b/dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.h
--- a/dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.h
+++ b/dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.h
@@ -125,7 +125,8 @@
 #endif
   }
 
-#ifdef MOZ_WIDGET_ANDROID
+#if defined(MOZ_WIDGET_ANDROID) || \
+    (defined(MOZ_USE_HWDECODE) && defined(MOZ_WIDGET_GTK))
   Maybe<MediaDataDecoder::PropertyValue> GetDecodeProperty(
       MediaDataDecoder::PropertyName aName) const override;
 #endif
